A thread that may no longer run stays on the queue it waited on.
A thread unbound while it waited would still take turns;
a thread names a queue only while its account and binding put it on one.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a thread names a queue it is not for

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -324,7 +324,7 @@ static void thread_settle(struct thread *t)
     const struct thread *l = has_time(t->balance) ? NULL : thread_lender(t);
     uint8_t queue = thread_queue(t, t->balance, l);
     bool joined = queue != QUEUE_NONE && (queue != t->queue || core != was);
-    if (queue != t->queue || core != was) {
+    if (queue != QUEUE_NONE && (queue != t->queue || core != was)) {
         if (t->queue != QUEUE_NONE) {
             ring_remove(queue_head(was, t->queue), t);
         }
